{"name":"Arylide Yellow","hex":"#e9d66b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arylide yellow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a family of organic compounds used as yellow pigments, obtained by azo coupling of aniline and acetoacetanilide or their derivatives."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arylide_yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arylide yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Arylide yellow, also known as Hansa yellow and monoazo yellow, is a family of organic compounds used as pigments. They are primarily used as industrial colorants including plastics, building paints and inks. They are also used in artistic oil paints, acrylics and watercolors. These pigments are usually semi-transparent and range from orange-yellow to yellow-greens. Related organic pigments are the diarylide pigments. Overall, these pigments have partially displaced the toxic cadmium yellow in the marketplace. Painters such as Alexander Calder and Jackson Pollock are known to have employed arylide yellow in their artworks."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arylide_yellow","wikidata":"Q4802709"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Aspen-PopulusTremuloides-2001-09-27.jpg/500px-Aspen-PopulusTremuloides-2001-09-27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Aspen-PopulusTremuloides-2001-09-27.jpg/1280px-Aspen-PopulusTremuloides-2001-09-27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Aspen-PopulusTremuloides-2001-09-27.jpg/500px-Aspen-PopulusTremuloides-2001-09-27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAspen-PopulusTremuloides-2001-09-27.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Ochre_quarry%2C_Roussillon%2C_France_%28465185258%29.jpg/500px-Ochre_quarry%2C_Roussillon%2C_France_%28465185258%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Ochre_quarry%2C_Roussillon%2C_France_%28465185258%29.jpg/500px-Ochre_quarry%2C_Roussillon%2C_France_%28465185258%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOchre_quarry%2C_Roussillon%2C_France_(465185258).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/20130304FeteDuCitronMenton_010.jpg/500px-20130304FeteDuCitronMenton_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/20130304FeteDuCitronMenton_010.jpg/1280px-20130304FeteDuCitronMenton_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","sr